- @next: A landslide victory for Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi and the INC.

@next
on-arrival: india_pm = "Rajiv Gandhi"; india_government = "INC"; 

Following the sudden assassination of Indira Gandhi, the popularity of her INC and her son the interim Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi. This combined with a general fear of growing instability has catapulted the INC to its largest victory ever since independence.

Voting in the states of Punjab and Assam have been delayed to an unknown time due to the Sikh insurgency and the "Anti-Foreigners Movement" respectively. 

It was already suspected that India under Indira was covertly supporting the Tamil militants and that assumption is likely to continue under Rajiv. Though it should be reminded that both Prime Ministers are far from proposing extraordinary measures such as a direct Indian intervention unlike politicians in Tamil Nadu like MGR.
